2026-10-19T22:24:26.4759206Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 57215
2026-10-19T22:24:26.4759497Z   ISSUE_TITLE: Plugin loader: a directory plugin with no root server or index entry loads nothing and gives no warning
2026-10-19T22:24:26.4761344Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Problem

A directory plugin with no root `server.ts|js` or `index.ts|js` loads nothing. The host gives no warning. The host also ignores the `exports` field of `package.json`.

## Source (v2.0.31)

- `packages/plugin/src/host.ts:43` tries only two names for the server entry:

  `return { server: entry(["server", ""]), tui: entry(["tui"]), rpc: entry(["rpc"]) }`

  For a directory with no package name, `entry` resolves `server` and `index` only.
- `packages/core/src/config/plugin/source.ts:167` discards the plugin without a message:

  `if (!entrypoints.server) return []`

## Purpose

A plugin author publishes a directory plugin. The `package.json` `exports` field gives the entry point. The plugin does not load. The author sees no error and no warning.

## Proposed minimal API

Resolve the entry through `package.json` `exports` when the root names are missing. If the resolution finds nothing, log a warning with the plugin path.

## What the plugin does today without it

The plugin does not load. The host stays silent. The author must debug the resolution by hand.

